<title>NORWAY: UBN 1996 profits fall.</title>
<headline>UBN 1996 profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31</p>
<p>				    (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income		     2,559	vs	2,781</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating profit		1,173	vs	1,406</p>
<p> Net profit				    851	vs	1,071</p>
<p>EPS 1996 (crowns)  Dividend 1996 (crowns)</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's biggest savings bank is Union Bank of Norway ASA, known locally as Sparebanken NOR. Six analysts polled by Reuters had forecast 1996 pre-tax operating profits of 1.23 billion crowns.</p>
<p> Non-interest operating income	 1,547	vs	1,299</p>
<p> Operating expenses			2,975	vs	2,648</p>
<p> Operating profit before losses	1,131	vs	1,432</p>
<p> Tax and minorities			  322	vs	  335</p>
<p> Proposed dividend 1996 (crowns)	  15	vs	  N/A</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
